<description>
The function `get_color_quant_mode` is an inline member function of the `symbolic_compressed_block` struct. It returns the value of the `quant_mode` member of the struct, which represents the color quantization method used for the block. The function itself is a simple accessor and does not perform any validation or transformation of the data.
</description>

<requirements>

<requirement>
The `this` pointer to the `symbolic_compressed_block` object must be a valid, non-null pointer. This is because the function directly dereferences this pointer to access the `quant_mode` member, and a null pointer would cause a crash.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `quant_mode` field of the `symbolic_compressed_block` struct should be initialized to one of the values from the `quant_method` enum (0-8). Although this function doesn't validate the value, subsequent processing of the returned value will likely assume it's within the valid range, and out-of-range values could lead to crashes or undefined behavior in other parts of the program.
</requirement>

</requirements>

</function-requirements>

